      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I get what OP has to say. It sucks joining a public world only to find out that everyone in the world is speaking another language you don't know.\n\nBeing able to see the majority of players localization or perhaps a chosen language option, in a world, would be beneficial for those who want to find people they can understand.\n\nYou have to realise that language is still a major barrier for many people, and no amount of just \"being social\" will change this. Unless you are actively trying to learn a new language.\n\nThe only way I could really see this being abused is by people who are being racist.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
